                          "text":  "I landed in January 2004 inside a wrapping of airbags, bounced across Gusev Crater and rolled to a stop. My mission was supposed to last 90 days. My twin, Opportunity, landed on the other side of the planet three weeks later.\n\nScientists hoped my crater was an old lakebed. At first all I found was dry lava. So I drove to the nearest hills, about three kilometres away, and climbed one. It took more than a year. I am a rover, not a mountain goat, but I got to the top.",
